        "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+7{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{1}^{2}+7\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{1}^{2}-2\\cdot x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{(2)^{4}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4})+7(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})-2(2-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{2}+\\frac{49}{3}-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{41}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
